{"id": "sdqa0100", "pool": "sdqa", "tier": "never", "audio_s": 4.4, "n_chunks": 5, "n_concurrent": 5, "gen_active_at_eot": true, "eot_score": 0.114, "eot_read_ms": 27, "reference_answer": "exerts control by switching heating or cooling devices on or off, or by regulating the flow of a heat transfer fluid as needed, to maintain the correct temperature", "query": "How do thermostats work?", "transcript": "How do thermostats work?", "mode": "local", "answer": "thermostat is a device that helps control the temperature in a room or building. It works by sensing the current temperature and turning heating or cooling systems on or off to maintain a set temperature. Most thermostats have a dial or digital display where you can set your desired temperature. When the actual temperature moves away from your set point, the thermostat sends a signal to the heating or cooling system to turn on or off, helping keep the space comfortable.", "answer_ms": 2777}
